msgid "catform.advanced.hint"
msgstr "Almost never needed. This is for auxiliary text that in the prompt must go <i>after</i> the closing <code>&lt;signal_category&gt;</code> as a separate block (for example, a reference of known phrases for transcription) — and not as one more rule paragraph inside it."

msgid "catform.advanced.title"
msgstr "Extra blocks for Full/Compact (rarely needed)"

msgid "catform.compact.copy"
msgstr "Copy from Full"

msgid "catform.compact.label"
msgstr "Compact — shortened version, fallback"

msgid "catform.help.compact"
msgstr "<b>Compact</b> — the same idea, but condensed: used only if the model could not confidently identify the categories on the first pass. You can build it by clicking \"Copy from Full\" and shortening it by hand."

msgid "catform.help.language"
msgstr "<b>The special word <code>__OUTPUT_LANGUAGE__</code></b> — if a rule needs to ask the model to write something (for example, in detail/rationale), do not name a specific language (\"write in Russian\") — the analysis may also run in English. Instead, insert <code>__OUTPUT_LANGUAGE__</code> literally — the server substitutes the right language before sending it to the model. It only works in Full/Compact; in Summary it is pointless, nothing substitutes it there. The \"Insert __OUTPUT_LANGUAGE__\" button next to the field does this without typos — nothing helps except an exact match: neither an extra space nor a different number of underscores will work, and the form will not let such text be saved and will tell you what is wrong."

msgid "catform.help.rules"
msgstr "<b>Rules (Full)</b> — a detailed description of the signs for the second, careful pass. Write them as separate paragraphs using the \"Add rule\" button — for example, one paragraph on what we are looking for in general, another with a list of specific signs, another on which combination of them counts as the signal being found and how it affects the risk level. The <code>&lt;signal_category&gt;</code> tag is wrapped around automatically — you do not need to write it yourself."

msgid "catform.help.scene"
msgstr "<b>Scene example</b> — optional; a ready-made analysis of a similar situation helps the model."

msgid "catform.help.summary"
msgstr "<b>Summary</b> — a short description in English for a quick first pass: what must be visible in the photo for the model to look closely at this category at all."

msgid "catform.help.title"
msgstr "How a category works — read before your first time"

msgid "catform.insert_placeholder"
msgstr "Insert __OUTPUT_LANGUAGE__"

